<figure class="jev-flow" aria-labelledby="jev-title" aria-describedby="jev-caption">
  <header class="flow-head">
    <span class="eyeline">FIELD NOTES / 01</span>
    <strong id="jev-title">From signal to response</strong>
    <p>Jev assesses. Code routes. Checks govern execution.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="flow-body">
    <div class="signal"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Monitoring</strong><span>New error pattern after a deployment</span></div>
    <div class="override"><span>PRIORITY RULE</span> Critical alert? Page on-call directly.</div>
    <div class="connector" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
    <section class="decision" aria-label="First Jev decision">
      <div class="step-label"><span>01 / JEV ASSESSMENT</span><span class="pill">AMBIGUOUS</span></div>
      <strong>Does this need investigation?</strong>
      <p>Logs + metrics + deployment context</p>
      <div class="probability"><span>P(actionable)</span><b>0.72</b></div>
      <div class="meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:72%"></span></div>
    </section>
    <div class="branches">
      <div class="branch"><span class="condition">↓ P &lt; 0.20</span><strong>Observe</strong><p>Recheck on a timer. Persistent errors return to assessment.</p></div>
      <div class="branch selected"><span class="condition">↓ P ≥ 0.20</span><strong>Investigate</strong><p>An LLM correlates evidence and proposes a diagnosis.</p><span class="path-tag">EXAMPLE PATH</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="connector continuation">From investigation ↓</div>
    <section class="decision" aria-label="Second Jev decision after investigation">
      <div class="step-label"><span>02 / JEV ASSESSMENT</span><span class="pill">AMBIGUOUS</span></div>
      <strong>Does an approved runbook apply?</strong>
      <p>Original evidence + investigation findings + runbook</p>
      <div class="probability"><span>P(applicable)</span><b>0.97</b></div>
      <div class="meter" aria-hidden="true"><span style="width:97%"></span></div>
    </section>
    <div class="branches">
      <div class="branch"><span class="condition">↓ P &lt; 0.95 OR checks fail</span><strong>Review</strong><p>Gather evidence or ask a human. Page if urgency requires it.</p></div>
      <div class="branch selected"><span class="condition">↓ P ≥ 0.95 AND checks pass</span><strong>Remediate</strong><p>Code verifies permissions and live preconditions before execution.</p><span class="path-tag">EXAMPLE PATH</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="connector continuation">After remediation ↓</div>
    <div class="verify"><span class="step-label">03 / EXECUTABLE HEALTH CHECKS</span><strong>Did the service recover?</strong><div class="outcomes"><span><b>PASS</b> Return to monitoring</span><span><b>FAIL</b> Stop automation and page</span></div></div>
    <p class="fallback">Missing or unusable model output → investigation or human review.</p>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="jev-caption">A proposed incident workflow. Scores and thresholds are illustrative, not measured or recommended operating values. Blue marks one example path; probabilities do not certify safety.</figcaption>
</figure>

